## Distribution Policy

Optimizations created in this product branch stay local unless the owner explicitly approves distribution.

## UI Direction

The tool UI must preserve the existing advertising-tool structure and be calibrated from the provided brand book, product links, product documents, logo, screenshots, or creative examples.

If brand materials are provided:

- Extract brand colors and use them as UI tokens.
- Adjust the top-left brand display, app name, badge, labels, defaults, examples, and empty states.
- Match product category, tone, and visual maturity without replacing the baseline layout.
- Use product-specific examples and labels.

If brand materials are missing:

- Use a restrained neutral palette.
- Mark UI palette as pending brand calibration.
- Ask again for brand book, screenshots, or product link before final visual delivery.

Do not remove the top bar, left configuration panel, right results area, Key/model management surface, model-pool controls, API call area, or scored result cards unless the owner explicitly approves that exception.
